                <pb facs="0325" n="226" sameAs="frus:frus1936v05/pg226"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">824.00/752: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Muccio</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-05-18T17:00:00-04:00">May 18, 1936—5 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>11. Repeat your 21, May 17, noon, to Buenos Aires for Braden<anchor n="8"
                        xml:id="d188-f1"/> as well as all subsequent telegrams reporting important
                    developments in the political situation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d188-f1" n="8" xml:id="d188-f1-content">
                <p>Spruille Braden, American delegate to the Chaco Peace Conference; see <ref
                        target="#pg35">pp. 35</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
